<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate") %>

<section class="content-hero contact-hero-img">
  <div class="cover contact-hero-inner">
    <div class="cover narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-dark">About SensiQ</span>
      <h1>Inclusive education that respects how people actually learn.</h1>
      <p>SensiQ is an e-learning experience shaped around accessibility first. We support learners who rely on alternative communication modes, assistive tools, and more thoughtful digital interaction.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="contact-hero-visual">
      <img src="/images/about_hero.png" alt="Diverse learners using inclusive assistive technology" class="contact-hero-image">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block section-light">
  <div class="cover two-column">
    <div class="content-card reveal">
      <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-bullseye" style="color:var(--blue)"></i> Our Mission</h2>
      <p>Remove barriers that keep sensory-disabled learners from participating fully in digital education. We believe every learner deserves equal access to knowledge, regardless of physical ability.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-card reveal">
      <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-rocket" style="color:var(--gold-deep)"></i> Our Vision</h2>
      <p>Build a platform where accessibility, dignity, and independence are standard parts of every learning path — not afterthoughts or optional features.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
  <div class="cover">
    <div class="section-heading reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-gold">Core Principles</span>
      <h2>How the Platform is Designed</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="principles-grid">
      <article class="principle-card reveal">
        <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-universal-access" style="color:var(--blue)"></i> Access First</h3>
        <p>Readable layouts, strong contrast, and assistive-friendly flows are part of the baseline — not add-ons.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card reveal">
        <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group" style="color:var(--blue)"></i> Multiple Modalities</h3>
        <p>Sign support, speech support, and text-first experiences work together rather than competing.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card reveal">
        <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-person-walking" style="color:var(--blue)"></i> Independent Learning</h3>
        <p>Learners should be able to navigate, understand, and continue their studies with minimal friction.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card reveal">
        <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-brain" style="color:var(--blue)"></i> AI-Powered Assistance</h3>
        <p>Speech recognition, natural language processing, and computer vision power the assistive tools behind the scenes.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block section-light">
  <div class="cover">
    <div class="section-heading reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-blue">Technology Stack</span>
      <h2>Academic Foundations</h2>
      <p>Each module is grounded in specific branches of Computer Engineering and related disciplines.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="principles-grid">
      <div class="content-card reveal">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-hands-asl-interpreting" style="color:var(--blue)"></i> Sign Language (HCI)</h2>
        <p>Video modules with ISL sign language content implemented using Human-Computer Interaction and Multimedia Systems principles.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-card reveal">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-microphone" style="color:var(--blue)"></i> Speech-to-Text (NLP)</h2>
        <p>Mute users benefit from speech recognition powered by Natural Language Processing and the Web Speech API.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-card reveal">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-volume-high" style="color:var(--blue)"></i> Text-to-Speech (AI)</h2>
        <p>Visually impaired learners access content through synthesized speech, powered by the SpeechSynthesis API.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-card reveal">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-hand" style="color:var(--blue)"></i> Text-to-Sign (CV)</h2>
        <p>Text content is converted to ISL fingerspelling using Computer Vision inspired mapping and animation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

